=== 1. GF(2^128) Splice Index-Set Derivation & Length-Floor Proofs (algebra.py) ===
GF(2^128) = GF(2)[x]/(x^128+x^7+x^2+x+1)   (COLM v1, PDF p.2, section 1.1)
  x is primitive: x^(2^128-1) = 1                                        OK
  x has order exactly 2^128-1 (x^(2^127) != 1)                           OK
  1/3 = 0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffffff82  (degree 127)
  3 * (1/3) = 1                                                          OK

[A] the FADE relation -- I0 is the support of f(x), shifted by one
  sum_{k in {1,2,3,8,129}} x^(k-1) = 0                                   OK
  equivalently  1 + x + x^2 + x^7 + x^128 = 0, i.e. f(x) = 0             OK
  shifted by s=1   : sum_{k in [2, 3, 4, 9, 130]} x^(k-1) = 0            OK
  shifted by s=7   : sum_{k in [8, 9, 10, 15, 136]} x^(k-1) = 0          OK
  shifted by s=50  : sum_{k in [51, 52, 53, 58, 179]} x^(k-1) = 0        OK

[B] the fade's MINIMUM message length
    a non-empty I0 with sum x^(k-1) = 0 exists iff {x^0..x^(l-2)} is GF(2)-dependent
      l = 127 : 126 powers, GF(2)-rank 126  ->  non-empty I0 exists: False
      l = 128 : 127 powers, GF(2)-rank 127  ->  non-empty I0 exists: False
      l = 129 : 128 powers, GF(2)-rank 128  ->  non-empty I0 exists: False
      l = 130 : 129 powers, GF(2)-rank 128  ->  non-empty I0 exists: True
      l = 131 : 130 powers, GF(2)-rank 128  ->  non-empty I0 exists: True
  no non-empty I0 for any l <= 129                                       OK
  a non-empty I0 exists at l = 130                                       OK
      kernel element derived by Gaussian elimination: x^128 = sum_{e in [0, 1, 2, 7]} x^e
      => I0 = [1, 2, 3, 8, 129]
  the DERIVED kernel element is exactly I0 = {1,2,3,8,129}               OK

[C] the TRANSPLANT relation
    A splice at block i moves the decryption onto query 2's state -- it makes
    X_mix[i] = X_2[i] and W_mix[i] = W_2[i] -- IF AND ONLY IF W_mix[i-1] = W_2[i-1].
    State transfer is therefore STICKY ALONG A CONTIGUOUS RUN of spliced blocks
    and is destroyed by any unspliced block in between.  The transplant needs
      (i)  a contiguous run {m, m+1, ..., l+1} of spliced blocks reaching the tag, and
      (ii) W_mix[m-1] = W_2[m-1], i.e. S cap {1..m-1} = supp(x^(m-1)/3)+1, possible
           only if maxdeg(x^(m-1)/3) <= m-2   -- 'condition (C)'.
  condition (C) first holds at m = 129                                   OK
  condition (C) fails for every m <= 128                                 OK
      x^128/3 has support [0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]  =>  prefix [1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
      at l = m = 129 the run is {129,130} = {l, l+1}, so S = [1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 129, 130]
  the DERIVED transplant set at l = 129 is exactly {1,3,4,5,6,7,129,130} OK
  for l > 129 the SAME prefix works and the run is simply {129..l+1}     OK
  condition (C) fails at m = 128 (deg(x^127/3) = 127 > 126)              OK
  m <= l forces l >= 129: no transplant exists below that                OK

[D] the COLM_tau obstruction -- why the same two queries do NOT reach COLM_127
  x^tau/3 in span{1..x^(tau-1)} for NO tau in 1..127 (degree is always 127) OK
      i.e. the blocking quantity 3^{-1} x^tau always has an x^127 term, so the
      intermediate tag's state difference can never be cancelled for tau <= 127.
      The margin is exactly one block: tau* = 128.

ALGEBRA: ALL CHECKS PASS

